- Welcome to Virgulas
  A guided tour you navigate, not a page you scroll. Zoom into a note to read it fully.
  + Read it by zooming
    Select a bullet, or press Alt+→, to zoom into a note. Alt+← comes back out.
  + Step from note to note
    ↓ and ↑ move. With nothing focused, ↓ starts at the first note.
  + Nothing is saved yet
    This tour lives in memory and disappears when the tab closes.

+ Move and zoom
  Four keys carry the whole navigation model. Try them as you read.
  + Select a note to edit it
    Click a note, type, then press Escape to go back to browsing.
  + Zoom in and out
    Alt+→ and Alt+← on desktop; tapping a bullet works everywhere.
  + Step between notes
    ↓ and ↑ move; with nothing focused, ↓ starts at the first note.

+ Everything here is editable
  This is a real document. Rewrite it, or delete it once you know the app.
  + Add a note
    Enter adds a note after this one, or the first child if it already has one.
  + Give a note a description
    Shift+Enter toggles between a note's title and its description.
  + Reshape the tree
    Tab indents, Alt+↑/↓ moves a note, Ctrl+Space folds its children.

+ Write with light markdown
  Descriptions render as markdown when you zoom in.
  Titles stay single lines; descriptions can be full documents.
  ## Headings, lists, quotes
  Body text supports **bold**, __italic__, `code`, and [links](https://virgulas.com).
  1. Ordered lists keep their numbers
  2. Rules separate ideas
  > Quotes set a passage apart.
  \---
  ```
  const idea = 'fenced code and tables too'
  ```
  | Markdown | Renders |
  | --- | --- |
  | Tables | Yes |
  + Tags and mentions become pills
    Type #project or @name, then select the pill to search that token.
  + Paste an outline as an outline
    Pasted bulleted text becomes notes, not one long line.

+ Find anything
  Escape with nothing focused opens search and hides what does not match.
  + Narrow as you type
    Lowercase ignores case; a single capital letter makes it exact.
  + Open a result
    Tab through the matches and press Enter to zoom to one.

+ Turn notes into tasks
  Mark work done, give it a due date, and let it repeat.
  - [ ] Plan the next review due:2026-09-15
    Overdue work is highlighted. Dates are written due:yyyy-MM-dd.
  - [ ] Pay rent due:2026-09-28 rec:1m
    rec:1m repeats monthly; completing it advances the date.
  + The Tasks panel
    Ctrl+Alt+K groups work into pending, scheduled, and done.

+ Capture on the go
  Collect a thought now and file it into your Inbox on the next unlock.
  + Share to Virgulas
    Long-press the app icon for Quick capture, or share from another app.
  + Capture from any page
    Options → Quick capture has a bookmarklet you can click anywhere.
  + A capture stays locked
    No passphrase, no decryption, no network; it queues on this device.

+ Choose where notes live
  This tour is in memory and vanishes when the tab closes. Keep it when ready.
  + Local
    Encrypted in this browser under a passphrase only you know.
  + Remote
    An account plus a separate passphrase syncs your devices.
  + File
    A plain .vmd file you own and can open anywhere.
  + How encryption works
    AES-GCM-256 under a PBKDF2 key of 600,000 iterations, per document.

+ Make it yours
  Theme, wide mode, backups, and the source code all live in Options.
  + Toggle the theme
    Ctrl+Alt+T switches theme; Ctrl+Alt+W widens the outline.
  + Back up a document
    Options → Data exports and imports .vmd files.
